    "result": "I implemented `plan_extraction` in `solution.py` following the spec, and wrote 23 tests in `tests/test_solution.py`. They all pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`. I didn't run a coverage check, so the 90% gate is untested here.\n\nThe function treats `\\` as a separator and drops empty and `.` segments. It rejects NUL characters, absolute paths, drive prefixes, any `..` that climbs above the destination, and members that are empty after normalisation. Directory entries are validated but left out of the result. File members that collide case-insensitively raise `UnsafePathError`, and a bad member anywhere means nothing is returned. The tests cover each of these rules, including that `1:x` is not treated as a drive prefix.",
